{
  "id": "Compound::DB00307 - Gene::6256",
  "verbalization": "Bexarotene is linked to Rxra through a series of molecular interactions that involve retinoids and their derivatives. The evidence suggests that Bexarotene, as part of the retinoid family, binds to Rxra, a key component in the retinoic acid receptor pathway. This connection is supported by the presence of Adapalene, a retinoid, which binds to Rxra, and the lowest common ancestor of Bexarotene and Adapalene is the Naphthalenes, indicating a shared structural or functional relationship. The evidence also highlights that Bexarotene can cause Dermatitis Irritant Contact, which is mediated by Adapalene, further reinforcing the role of Rxra in these interactions. The integration of these pathways suggests that Bexarotene exerts its effects on Rxra through retinoid signaling, potentially modulating cellular processes related to skin inflammation and receptor activation.",
